# DIAGNOSTICS

`vx_debug_write` returns:

: `VX_OK`
  The bytes are written, or held in the line buffer.
: `VX_ERR_ACCESS`
  The calling task may not write.
: `VX_ERR_INVALID`
  Part of <s> is not readable memory of the caller's.
  It is copied 256 bytes at a time, and what came before the bad part is written.

# BUGS

The design allows the call only while the task holds a debug capability (01 §3); today every task descends from the root task, so every task may write.

Nothing reads the kernel's log from user space yet.

Bytes of a line with no newline stay in the thread's buffer, and are lost if the thread exits.
